# Complete desktop action icon glossary
Workstream-ID: lea-34
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/34
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed bounded public documentation request
Status: DONE
Milestone: Explain every desktop action icon in README and the user reference
Dependencies: lea-33

## Purpose
Make all 36 native action icons discoverable with their actual artwork,
displayed names and source-grounded meanings. Explain the semantic colors and
steady border glow without confusing operations with confirmed outcomes.

## Tasks
- [x] Review the complete state, artwork, palette and authoritative stage sources.
- [x] Export the exact original artwork as public-safe documentation assets.
- [x] Add all icons and meanings to an expandable README glossary.
- [x] Add the detailed grouped reference with state IDs, colors and caveats.
- [x] Link the reference from the desktop and contributor guides.
- [x] Verify complete coverage, matching labels/meanings, images and navigation.
- [x] Reconcile the scoped issue, Project status and persistent backlink.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] README and documentation show every one of the 36 actual native designs.
- [x] Every icon has its exact displayed name and a plain-English explanation.
- [x] The detailed reference includes all state IDs and correct semantic tones.
- [x] Input pauses, timed waits, selection/upload and attempts/outcomes stay distinct.
- [x] All documentation SVGs render and directly affected relative links resolve.
- [x] One issue-backed Project item and durable backlink represent this workstream.
- [x] Runtime code, installed applications, private setup and existing releases stay unchanged.

## Completion evidence
Authoring covers the seven lifecycle states and 29 engine operations from
`gui/activity.py::_STATES`, using exact `gui/activity_icons.py::_ARTWORK`
geometry and Harbor Daylight palette values. All explanatory content is
public-safe product behavior; no applicant or runtime data is included.
All 36 exported SVGs render through Qt and match the native vector bodies,
labels and semantic tones. All 126 relative references across the four affected
guides resolve. Both locally rendered Markdown glossaries load every icon and
matching explanation in an isolated browser; the README disclosure and
1280px/390px page containment pass. Directly inspect the full icon sheet and
expanded README layout. These are local documentation checks, not a hosted
GitHub page, live LinkedIn qualification or human acceptance.

Scoped synchronization creates issue #34 and one issue-backed Project item,
then writes the persistent backlink. Independent read-back verifies the exact
managed description and membership, all 34 backlinks and unchanged snapshots,
mappings and local source records for all 33 predecessors. Completion remains
local documentation delivery, not publication. No new commit, push, release,
live LinkedIn action or application restart is included.

